BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fledge Fest 2026
DTSTART:20260822T110000
DTEND:20260822T233000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:b60947efdf913d5481dfaa4e330018@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:You’re invited to the fourth annual Fledge Fest\, hosted by 
 Fledgling Farmstead in Tunbridge. Fledge Fest is an all-ages\, community-m
 inded\, music and arts event. Our mission is to nurture community vibrancy
  through live music\, the arts\, and local food at an affordable price. Co
 me for part of the event\, or bring your tent and stay for the weekend! Fl
 edge Fest aims to feature some of the best local food offerings\, up-and-c
 oming musicians from a wide selection of genres\, skills shares and though
 tful workshops\, and interactive art installations. This event is also a f
 undraiser! A portion of this year's proceeds will go to NOFA-VT's Farmer E
 mergency Fund and Fledgling Farmstead's 2027 CSA subsidy fund. Friday’s 
 event is free\, kicking off with a community potluck featuring roasted lam
 b raised on the farm\, followed by a contra dance with Laussane Allen as c
 aller and the Wailing Coywolves Contraband. At dusk\, we will screen two s
 horts from the film project\, Campfire Stories\, featuring a few of the lo
 vely portraits of sustainable living by filmmaker Mattias Olsson. Finally
 \, local naturalist Cheryl Metcalf will lead a moth observation night to r
 ound out Friday evening. Saturday is a ticketed event\, gates open at 11 a
 nd music starting at 1. Festival goers are invited to come early to join u
 s for yoga\, a native edible plant walk\, immersive conversations about co
 mmunity resiliency\, hands-on seed saving workshop\, fiber work\, block pr
 inting\, and more! Forest art installations\, including art from Bread and
  Puppet founder\, Peter Schumann\, encourage visitors to explore the stunn
 ing hilltop event space\, while our lawn games\, story walk\, and children
 's Forest Playground offer something for all ages. Performances by twelve 
 Vermont- and New-England-based artists offer music\, dance\, and theater f
 or all tastes\, while Vermont-based food trucks serve up Korean-inspired s
 treet food\, wood-fired locavore dinner\, and gelato. Beer\, wine\, and no
 n-alcoholic drinks from Foxy's of Barre\, and a bonfire and late-night DJ 
 wrap up the evening. On site camping available. Sliding scale starting at 
 $20\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fledgling Farmstead\, 213 Bicknell Hill Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/fledge-fes
 t-2026-02-08-2026-21-34-16
END:VEVENT
