BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hot Sauce Making Class with Butterfly Bakery of Vermont
DTSTART:20260822T130000
DTEND:20260822T150000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:07b55178b211793e50513b7c9068de@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Ever wondered what goes into making a great hot sauce? Join Bu
 tterfly Bakery of Vermont founder Claire Georges for a hands-on exploratio
 n of the art\, science\, and flavor of hot sauce making. Learn how to choo
 se and balance flavors\, work with peppers\, safely bottle hot sauce for g
 ifting or sale\, and create delicious sauces of your own to take home. Whe
 ther you're a backyard gardener with more peppers than you know what to do
  with\, a hot sauce enthusiast\, or simply curious about food production\,
  you'll leave with practical knowledge\, insider tips\, and a deeper appre
 ciation for the craft behind every bottle. This class is part of Butterfly
  Bakery of Vermont’s 2026 Pepper Patron campaign. Once a year\, BBVT buy
 s peppers for the year directly from small farms across Vermont and beyond
 . Through the Pepper Patron campaign\, supporters help make that harvest p
 ossible while getting closer to the farms\, the peppers\, and the story be
 hind every bottle. Cost: $150 per person To learn more or to register\, vi
 sit https://butterflybakeryvt.com/pages/2026-pepper-crowdfund\, email info
 @butterflybakeryvt.com or call 802-243-4545.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Butterfly Bakery of Vermont\, 698 S. Barre Rd.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/hot-sauce-
 making-class-with-butterfly-bakery-of-vermont-02-06-2026-14-58-09
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Independence Upon the Water: Lake Champlain\, Isle La Motte\, and 
 the Making of a Nation
DTSTART:20260822T100000
DTEND:20260822T110000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:baba7e997b8ed6c1fa7957d54e27b2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The story of the American Revolution is often told through the
  streets of Boston\, the halls of Philadelphia\, and the battlefields of L
 exington\, Concord\, and Yorktown. Yet one of the nation's most important 
 frontiers lay hundreds of miles to the north along the waters of Lake Cham
 plain. Join us as historian Jonathan C. Lane from Revolution 250 - the Com
 monwealth of Massachusetts' 250th Anniversary commission - explores the pi
 votal role that Lake Champlain and Isle La Motte played in America's strug
 gle for independence. From the capture of Fort Ticonderoga and Benedict Ar
 nold's improvised fleet to the Saratoga campaign and Benjamin Franklin and
  Charles Carroll's diplomatic mission to Montreal and finally the settleme
 nt of Vermont's northern frontier\, discover how control of this vital wat
 erway helped shape the course of the Revolution and secure the future of t
 he United States. As we commemorate the 250th Anniversary of the American 
 Revolution\, let us rediscover the remarkable people\, places\, and events
  that transformed a remote frontier into an essential chapter in the makin
 g of a nation. The ILM 250th Anniversary Commission events are supported i
 n part by the Vermont Humanities\, the state affiliate of the National End
 owment for the Humanities\, www.vermonthumanities.org\, in partnership wit
 h the Vermont 250th Anniversary Commission\, https://anniversary250.vermon
 t.gov. Special thanks to the Isle La Motte Preservation Trust for hosting 
 this event as a part of Isle La Motte Celebrates Our Independence's Commem
 oration Day activities. More information is available at https://islelamot
 te.us/ilm250/.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Goodsell Ridge Preserve Visitor Center\, 239 Quarry Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/independen
 ce-upon-the-water-lake-champlain-isle-la-motte-and-the-making-of-a-nation-
 08-08-2026-20-34-10
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jason and the Argonauts
DTSTART:20260822T150000
DTEND:20260822T164500
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:f284b287cff3fd7bdf16a01b3f61f6@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Before there was Christopher Nolan’s The Odyssey… “Some 
 say Citizen Kane is the greatest motion picture of all time. Other say it
 ’s Casablanca. For me\, the greatest picture of all time is Jason and th
 e Argonauts.” —Tom Hanks\, presenting Ray Harryhausen with an honorary
  Oscar in 1992. A brave man and his shipload of followers heedlessly throw
  themselves into one dangerous adventure after another\, as vengeful gods 
 mark their progress. Nah\, forget Christopher Nolan\, we’re talking abou
 t Don Chaffey’s 1963 masterpiece\, Jason and the Argonauts. If Films-Mad
 e-From-Ancient-Greek-Texts Fever has you in its sway\, you need to see thi
 s. The basics of the story are pretty well-known: Jason and his backing ba
 nd\, the Argonauts\, seek the Golden Fleece. His lover\, Medea\, is quite 
 a handful. Zeus is unhappy\, Hera digs our hero\, and Hercules shows up\, 
 too. But who are we kidding—the star of this show is Ray Harryhausen\, t
 he undisputed master of stop-motion effects in motion pictures. Many consi
 der this film to be his masterwork. The great man’s inimitable effects a
 ppear in one epic scene after another here: the towering bronze giant Talo
 s\, the vulturous harpies\, the seven-headed serpent Hydra\, and\, most fa
 mously\, that terrifying army of skeletons! Given the painstaking work nec
 essary for stop-motion effects\, the battle between the four humans and se
 ven skeleton creatures took four months to execute. The film\, which manag
 ed to escape right-wing furor on its release 1963— surprising considerin
 g its lack of fealty to the original third-century Greek poem (unless\, ma
 ybe\, “featly to the original text” isn’t what the furor is really a
 bout)—was a major hit upon its release\, and its reputation has only gro
 wn since. For all the special-effects mayhem\, the movie was rated G\, so 
 by all means bring the kids. It’s a Saturday matinee\, after all!\n\nSou
 rces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Main Street Landing Film House\, 60 Lake St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/jason-and-
 the-argonauts-11-08-2026-15-26-05
END:VEVENT
