SUMMARY:Splash Dance: DJ GAYBAR
DTSTART:20260822T130000
DTEND:20260822T150000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:a47ac09aea4b51618fd61a6b7fe639@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:GAYBAR is a Winooski-based queer DJ originally from the east c
 oast of Canada. Playing a mix of tech house\, drum & bass\, electronic\, a
 nd pop\, she has become a familiar presence at local events and festivals.
  She is a recurring performer for Queer Takeover at Radio Bean\, is known 
 for bringing the dance party to Emoji Nightmare-produced shows at Higher G
 round and is a resident DJ at drum & bass monthly SPARKOMATIK which takes 
 place at the Monkey House. Delighted kids and their caregivers soak up som
 e serious summer fun with a DJ-fueled dance party in City Hall Park's inte
 ractive\, wheelchair accessible splash fountain. Summer in the City is mad
 e possible in part thanks to Underwriters at the Pomerleau Family Foundati
 on\; Supporters Burlington Telecom\, Myti\, Soundtoys\, and Lake Champlain
  Chocolates\, and Community Partner American Flatbread Burlington & Mother
 ship Brewery. Media Sponsors: Seven Days and WCAX.⁠\n\nSources: Vermont.
 com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Burlington City Arts\, Burlington\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/splash-dan
 ce-dj-gaybar-19-06-2026-20-21-12
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twilight Series: Night Protocol with April Patterson Clemens & Cob
 alt Tobert
DTSTART:20260822T180000
DTEND:20260822T210000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:bf2ce2d6212adbacc37ba0f2546b04@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:6PM: Opening act April Patterson Clemens is a Vermont-based in
 die folk singer-songwriter from Texas and Cobalt Tolbert is a French Ameri
 can singer-guitarist who’s been rocking around Europe and the East Coast
  for over a decade. Tolbert adds flare and style to April's roster of orig
 inal songs with his versatile guitar playing and exquisite ear. Together\,
  they bring to life April's extensive and ever-expanding catalog of tunes.
  Seven Days said\, “When she sings\, Clemens channels medieval spirits w
 ith a rich\, earthy tone that bends itself ethereally\, the way water bend
 s an image. Ghosts seem to wander through one song to the next on the cont
 rolled quiver of Clemens’ voice.” Headliner Night Protocol was created
  to unite the sounds of the past\, present\, and future with a cutting-edg
 e style of electronic music. Night Protocol shows are driven by live analo
 g synthesizers\, pulsing basslines\, ripping guitar solos\, soaring saxoph
 one leads\, and harmonized vocals. Their live show takes a theatrical appr
 oach to music performance with coordinated visuals\, lighting effects\, an
 d a contagious sense of passion and energy for the foundations of electron
 ic music. Since founding in 2017\, Night Protocol have released two albums
  and two EPs to critical acclaim. They are set to release a new album in s
 ummer 2026 with songs that push the boundaries of the genre and stretch in
 to new territory as they unite both electronic music and live jam audience
 s. Lounge on the lawn as the sun dips low and enjoy live music with lumina
 ries from all corners of the Vermont music scene. Twilight Concerts light 
 up the park once (or twice) a month. Summer in the City is made possible i
 n part thanks to Underwriters at the Pomerleau Family Foundation\; Support
 ers Burlington Telecom\, Myti\, Soundtoys\, and Lake Champlain Chocolates
 \, and Community Partner American Flatbread Burlington & Mothership Brewer
 y. Media Sponsors: Seven Days and WCAX.⁠\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:City Hall Park\, 135 Church st
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/twilight-s
 eries-night-protocol-with-april-patterson-clemens-amp-cobalt-tobert-19-06-
 2026-20-21-48
END:VEVENT
