BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:World Soccer Festival 2026
DTSTART:20260822T090000
DTEND:20260822T140000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:59206600c5a7f5536c8676e47dcc7f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The 14th annual\, 3rd in Montpelier\, World Soccer Festival 20
 26 will take place on Saturday\, August 22\, 2026\, at Montpelier High Sch
 ool from 9 AM to 2 PM. This community-building event celebrates the game w
 e all love and the growing diversity in Vermont. This event is brought tog
 ether through a shared love of soccer\, music\, and food. There will be lo
 cal and international food vendors and fun activities for children of all 
 ages. This is a non-profit event with a focus on kids entering 2nd through
  8th grades\, featuring 3v3 friendly games and an adult international exhi
 bition game\, pitting the Capital Soccer Men’s team against the Central 
 America Stars. Each year\, teams get to represent a nation of their choice
 . All players on a team receive their country’s flag\, and a vibrant par
 ade of players kicks off the festival. This community-filled event celebra
 tes diversity and the “beautiful game” through music\, featuring Shida
 a Projects and Sambatucada. Visit worldsoccerfestival.org for more informa
 tion. Registration opens July 1st.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Montpelier High School\, 5 High School Drive
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/world-socc
 er-festival-2026-10-07-2026-20-40-11
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You're a Good Man\, Charlie Brown
DTSTART:20260822T110000
DTEND:20260822T123000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:526ff27a061b06933617dec7d44d42@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Based on the beloved Peanuts comic strip by Charles M. Schulz
 \, this charming musical brings Charlie Brown\, Snoopy\, Lucy\, Linus\, an
 d the rest of the gang to life in a heartwarming celebration of friendship
 \, imagination\, and the joys of everyday life. This production will be pe
 rformed outdoors in a partially shaded area. Chair seating will be availab
 le\; however\, a reservation does not guarantee a chair. Audience members 
 are encouraged to bring a blanket or lawn chair for their comfort.\n\nSour
 ces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Waypoint Center\, 31 School St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/youre-a-go
 od-man-charlie-brown-21-07-2026-15-12-26
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aug 23 | Hidden Brain: The Perceptions Tour
DTSTART:20260823T180000
DTEND:20260823T200000
DTSTAMP:20260822T114037Z
UID:29cef9d1cca294df68ed8a2d663553@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Are there parts of our minds that are hidden from us? This que
 stion launched the Hidden Brain podcast ten years ago. Since then\, Hidden
  Brain has helped millions of listeners accomplish their goals\, improve t
 heir relationships\, and develop a deeper understanding of their emotions.
  Now\, host and creator Shankar Vedantam brings seven key insights from th
 e first decade of Hidden Brain to the stage. Whether you’re new to the s
 how or a longtime listener\, this evening of science and storytelling will
  change how you think about yourself. Come share your own thoughts and ide
 as with Shankar and other fans of the show! This event is made possible wi
 th support from Saint Michael's College .\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Flynn\, 153 Main St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/aug-23-hid
 den-brain-the-perceptions-tour-27-05-2026-07-50-45
END:VEVENT
